  "comparison_sha": "ec335c39e4c241df40d0a920067682f8201f323c",
  "methodology": "Scope: compare first-success PR caches (before) against per-revision caches (after).\nBoth policies build the same frozen working-tree snapshot with the same Swift toolchain defaults, macOS batching, test concurrency, complete test suite and all-product release builds.\nDedicated push workflow emulates the two PR cache lifecycles within its own branch/cache namespace; it does not benchmark PR merge-ref provenance or SDK cache-key invalidation.\nRound 1: no cache; full dependency/product debug build, test build and complete suite, release build.\nRound 2: comment-only source revision in HomeswiftMCP; restore round 1 in both policies. Before retains first successful cache, after saves the updated revision.\nRound 3: comment-only source revision in the independent ElgatoKeyLights plugin; before restores round 1, after restores round 2. Tests and products are otherwise identical.\nEvery job performs five comment-only PluginHost.swift edits and all-product debug rebuilds, restoring the exact source afterward. Cache is saved before this probe, so probe artifacts never affect later cache revisions.\nCold compilation timings are controls, not expected cache-policy improvements. Each policy gets an independent hosted runner, so compare cautiously; shared-runtime guard uses repeated samples and follow-up verification for apparent regressions.\n",
  "limitations": [
    "Independent hosted runners; cold identical-code differences demonstrate substantial machine noise.",
    "Build/test/release/cache subtotals exclude runner queue, checkout, package installation, restart/asset checks and benchmark probes.",
    "macOS normal PR CI skips release; its debug/test/cache subtotal is also reported.",
    "The final repeat pins the same original and refreshed cache inputs after fixing truncated failure logs.",
    "Cache identity and PR merge-ref provenance are not performance-tested by this push-based policy simulation."
  ],
  "failures": [
